    "q-12633": {
      "dom_id": "step-q12633",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "What is the slope of a line that passes through the points $(0,3)$ and $(5,6)?$",
      "worked_solution": "We let $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(0,3)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(5,6),$ and compute the slope using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6-3}{5-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the slope is $m=\\frac{3}{5}.$",
