    "q-12629": {
      "dom_id": "step-q12629",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Calculate the slope of the line that passes through the points $(3,4)$ and $(2,4).$",
      "worked_solution": "We let $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(3,4)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(2,4),$ and compute the slope using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4-4}{2-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{-1} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the slope is $m=0.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
